# Copy to .env and load with: node --env-file=.env bin/autorouter.mjs claude
AUTOROUTER_AUTH_MODE=subscription
AUTOROUTER_CLIENT_PROFILE=compatible
# Jev remains the default evaluator. Ollama is experimental; see settings below.
AUTOROUTER_EVALUATOR=jev
# The launcher enables the router status line for this session. Set 0 to keep your own.
AUTOROUTER_STATUSLINE=1
# Optional metadata logs on stderr. Redirect stderr to a file when using the UI.
# AUTOROUTER_DEBUG=1
# Required for Jev only; subscription + Ollama needs no API keys.
TYPESAFE_API_KEY=
# For API billing instead, set AUTOROUTER_AUTH_MODE=api-key and fill this in.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Model IDs are configurable independently of the tier policy.
AUTOROUTER_HAIKU_MODEL=claude-haiku-4-5-20251001
AUTOROUTER_SONNET_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5
AUTOROUTER_OPUS_MODEL=claude-opus-5-5
AUTOROUTER_JEV_MODEL=jev-latest
AUTOROUTER_JEV_TIMEOUT_MS=1500
# Only suspicious context sizes need counting; this overlaps the evaluator.
AUTOROUTER_TOKEN_COUNT_TIMEOUT_MS=1500
AUTOROUTER_MIN_CONFIDENCE=0.75

# Experimental local evaluator in AutoRouter 0.3.1+: native decision API only.
# Install/start Ollama 0.35+, then run:
# claude-autorouter setup --evaluator ollama --pull --force
# Defaults to nimble:9b-q4_K_M (~5.63 GB download); --force replaces user config.
# Existing downloads are kept. Replace Qwen config/environment values from 0.2.0.
# All local models use /v1/systemone; custom tags/aliases must support that API.
# Add --ollama-model LOCAL_TAG_OR_ALIAS to setup to choose another suitable model.
# Tev1 alternatives use the same native API; choose one explicitly:
# claude-autorouter setup --evaluator ollama --ollama-model tev1:0.8b --pull --force
# AUTOROUTER_OLLAMA_TIMEOUT_MS=15000 claude-autorouter setup --evaluator ollama --ollama-model tev1:4b-q4_K_M --pull --force
# Downloads: Tev1 0.8B Q8 ~812 MB; Tev1 4B Q4_K_M ~2.7 GB.
# tev1:latest / tev1:4b select ~4.5 GB Q8; model terms: https://ollama.com/library/tev1
# Or set AUTOROUTER_EVALUATOR=ollama above and configure an installed model:
# AUTOROUTER_OLLAMA_URL=http://127.0.0.1:11434
# AUTOROUTER_OLLAMA_MODEL=nimble:9b-q4_K_M
# Unreleased source defaults: Tev1 0.8B/custom 1500ms; Tev1 4B 15000ms; Nimble 30000ms.
# An explicit timeout (including an old saved 1500) always overrides the default.
# Setup, doctor and startup show the effective model/deadline in unreleased source.
# Set only when intentionally overriding; Jev's separate deadline is unchanged:
# AUTOROUTER_OLLAMA_TIMEOUT_MS=30000
# AUTOROUTER_OLLAMA_KEEP_ALIVE=5m
# npm 0.3.1 still defaults all local models to 1500ms. Immediate launch workarounds:
# AUTOROUTER_OLLAMA_TIMEOUT_MS=15000 claude-autorouter claude  # selected Tev1 4B
# AUTOROUTER_OLLAMA_TIMEOUT_MS=30000 claude-autorouter claude  # selected Nimble
# The launcher primes the classifier before opening Claude, allowing up to 60s.
# Warmup and metadata-only doctor checks do not certify speed or accuracy.
# Native model context is retained; evaluator state stays capped at 3,000 bytes.
# Unreleased source omits Claude executor system instructions; task/history remain.
# After the idle period, cold reloading may exceed the deadline and use fallback.
# A longer keep-alive holds the model in memory longer but avoids some reloads.
# Native entropy confidence is not calibrated accuracy and does not use Jev's threshold.
# Historical measurements before these unreleased source fixes:
# On the tested M4, all 12 Nimble tuning requests exceeded the 1,500 ms deadline.
# Tev1 0.8B: 18/24 labels, 450 ms median; 4B: 22/24, 3.15s at a 10s deadline.
# Both Tev1 tags have a 2,050-token native context window; see measured limits.
# Source-only regression: node scripts/test-ollama-routing.mjs --model tev1:0.8b
# Uses local inference only; no Anthropic/Jev calls, downloads or config writes.
# A fallback timeout is not a valid Sonnet decision; mismatches fail the regression.
# See docs/ollama-evaluation.md before allowing slower local classifications.

AUTOROUTER_PORT=8787
# Required only for standalone `serve`; the `claude` launcher generates one.
AUTOROUTER_TOKEN=
